    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1966-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(\\log_8 2=\\frac{1}{3}\\) and \\(\\log_2 8=3.\\) Therefore \\(x=(\\frac{1}{3})^3=3^{-3},\\) so \\(\\log_3x=-3.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate \\(\\log_8 2\\) and \\(\\log_2 8\\) separately",
        "Express the resulting power as a power of \\(3\\)"
